<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Mstislavl</h1><p class="st-meta">1359 CE – 1529 CE (approx.) · capital Mstislavl</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An appanage of the Grand Duchy of Lithuania in eastern Belarus, ruled by descendants of Algirdas until 1529.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mstislavl">Mstislavl</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sozh-river">Sozh</a>, was a town of the old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smolensk">Smolensk</a> lands. After the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a> took it in the mid 14th century, it was given as an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> to sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algirdas">Algirdas</a>, first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karigaila">Karigaila</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lengvenis">Lingvenis</a>, whose descendants ruled it for over a century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mstislavl">Mstislavl</a> was a frontier principality facing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smolensk">Smolensk</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, with a largely <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> Ruthenian population. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lengvenis">Lingvenis</a>, who ruled from about 1390 to 1431, also served as a commander in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veliky-novgorod">Novgorod</a> and fought at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-grunwald">Grunwald</a>. His line, and later the Mstislavsky family through marriage, held the land as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of the grand duke.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1526 Prince Fyodor Mstislavsky fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, where his family became leading boyars. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mstislavl">Mstislavl</a> reverted to the grand duke, and in 1529 it lost its separate status, later becoming the Mstislavl Voivodeship.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1359 CE – 1529 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:86.75%;width:3.38%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1359 CE – 1529 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mstislavl</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Karigaila, Lingvenis, Yury Lingvenevich</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ruthenian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/belarus">Belarus</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mstsislaw Principality</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1444&amp;focus=principality-of-mstislavl" aria-label="Principality of Mstislavl on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5382 324 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Mstislavl lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5702 580L5556 562"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5556 562h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5702 580h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5702 580h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1444&amp;focus=principality-of-mstislavl">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
